From: HeMAiA
Subject: [PATCH] One division register per clock domain

Besides the packed division registers (four domains per 32-bit register,
loaded by CLOCK_VALID_REGISTER), every domain gets its own division register
DOMAIN_DIVISION_C<i> at 0x38 + 8i (nothing at 0x3c + 8i) and a valid register
of their own, DOMAIN_DIVISION_VALID at 0x34. A valid bit takes the division
of its domain from its own register set in the cycle it is written; the
divider loads it at its next count boundary. Both valid registers are
external (hwext) so that the controller sees the write in that cycle.
With +clk_div_log the simulation lists every division a valid bit takes.

